<td class="text"><div style="margin-bottom:6pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">During the fiscal quarter ended October&#160;2, 2026, none of our Directors or officers (as defined in Rule 16a-1(f) under the Exchange Act) adopted or terminated a &#8220;Rule 10b5-1 trading arrangement&#8221; or a &#8220;non-Rule 10b5-1 trading arrangement,&#8221; as each term is defined in Item 408 of Regulation S-K, except as follows:</span></div><div><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Henrique Braun, Chief Executive Officer, adopted a Rule 10b5-1 trading arrangement on August&#160;28, 2026 for the potential exercise of vested stock options and the associated sale of up to 136,968 shares of common stock of the Company, subject to certain conditions. The arrangement&#8217;s expiration date is August&#160;28, 2028, or such earlier date upon which all transactions are completed. His trading plan was adopted during an open trading window.</span></div><span></span>
